  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "SkGifCodec::haveDecodedRow",
    "file": "skia/src/codec/SkGifCodec.cpp",
    "description": "Heap OOB write is caused by passing an unchecked GIF frame row width into swizzling. In haveDecodedRow(), width/xEnd are validated against image bounds, but applyXformRow() is still called with rowBegin for the full frame row, and swizzle_index_to_n32() writes dst[x] for its computed dstWidth without enforcing that this fits the allocated destination row (especially with xOffset + frame width interactions). The missing clamp/consistency check between frame row span and swizzler destination span allows a 4-byte write past the bitmap allocation.",
    "conditions": "Trigger with a crafted GIF in android_codec path where decoded frame metadata (notably xOffset/frame width and possibly sampling) makes the row span used by swizzler exceed the actual writable pixels in the destination buffer. Harness flow: FuzzAndroidCodec -> SkAndroidCodec::getAndroidPixels -> SkGifCodec::decodeFrame -> haveDecodedRow -> applyXformRow -> SkSwizzler::swizzle -> swizzle_index_to_n32. A tiny malformed GIF (as provided) is sufficient; when swizzler width/offset derived from frame data is inconsistent with allocated output row size, the final pixel write overruns by 4 bytes."
  },
